# Backend: Python + FastAPI (hand-written code in generated hosts)

Source: `docs/backend/python-fastapi.md`. Contract: `docs/api-contract.md`. Decisions: `docs/backend/python-fastapi.md` § Kararlar. A host may copy this file into its own `.cursor/rules/`.

## Files you may and may not edit

- Never edit a file whose first line is `# <auto-generated by Generator />` (`*_generated.py`, `api/routers_generated.py`, `api/indexes_generated.py`): it is rewritten on every generate. Change the model in the Generator (model editor / manifest) and generate instead. Removing the header makes the file yours and the Generator skips it from then on — only as a last resort, and say so.
- Never edit `src/<pkg>/core/crud/**`, `core/http/**`, `core/errors/app_error.py`, `core/errors/common_codes.py` in a host: they are Generator assets, identical in every host. A fix goes into `src/generator-assets/python-fastapi/core/**` in the Generator and is copied byte for byte (relative imports inside assets only).
- K files (created once, then yours): `modules/<m>/{__init__,model,repository,hooks,service}.py`, `tests/modules/<m>/test_admin_crud.py`, `api/main.py`, `api/deps.py`, `core/config.py`, `core/db.py`, `worker/main.py`. Hand-written only: `admin_router.py`, `router.py`, `jobs.py`, feature modules without G files.

## Where code goes

- Business rules of an entity: `hooks.py` (`<E>Hooks(<E>HooksBase)`). `before_create(doc, body)` / `before_update(current, changes, body)` / `before_delete(current)` may change `doc` / `changes` or raise `AppError(code, message)` to stop. `after_*` cannot roll back: checks that must hold go in `before_*`. `map_rows(rows)` gets a whole page in one call (batch IO, no N+1); return rows in the same order. A field marked `access.computed` (live price …) is never stored and has no filter / sort: fill it in `map_rows`. A heavy `access.detailOnly` field is not read for list pages (`None` there); getOne returns it. `default_sort()` / `before_list(query, body)` / `before_get_by_id(query)` scope reads. The admin making the request: `current_actor()` from `core.crud` (id or `None` outside a request), e.g. `doc["createdBy"] = current_actor()`.
- Service: `service.py` keeps `class <E>Service(<E>ServiceBase)` and `build_<m>_service(db)`; generated routers and jobs build the service through it. Extra methods here; CRUD bodies stay in `CrudService`.
- Queries: `repository.py` (`<E>Repository(<E>RepositoryBase)`); only `core/db.py` imports the Mongo driver (`Database` alias; Motor today, PyMongo Async later), so use only calls both drivers share (`find`, `to_list(length=…)`, `insert_one`, …).
- Non-CRUD admin endpoints: `admin_router.py` with `route_class=ContractRoute`, `AdminDep` / `DbDep` from `api.deps`, responses via `contract_ok(...)`; include the router in `api/main.py`. Public endpoints: `router.py`. Jobs: `jobs.py`, registered in `worker/main.py`.
- Errors: raise `AppError` with contract codes (`core/errors/common_codes.py`) or project codes in the host's own `core/errors/codes.py` (K, create it when needed; 460–479 for 4xx-type, 560–579 for 5xx-type); never return error dicts or raise bare `HTTPException` from services.

## Rules

- Layers: `api/`, `worker/` → `modules/` → `core/` (and `engine/` / `integrations/` below modules when the host has them). A module imports another module's `service` / `model` only — never its `repository*`, `admin_router*`, `router` or `jobs`. `uv run lint-imports` must stay green.
- Absolute imports in host code (`<pkg>.core.crud`, `<pkg>.modules.<m>.service`); relative imports only inside assets.
- Wire shape: rows leave through the generated `Row` models (`to_wire`: `_id` → `id`, dates `….fffZ`, decimals as strings); hidden fields never appear in a response. Do not build response dicts by hand for CRUD data.
- Update semantics are JSON Merge Patch (api-contract §5): omitted = unchanged, `null` clears an optional single field, `null` on a required field / list is 400. Hooks see `changes` with `None` meaning "unset".
- Document and sub-object models are `extra="forbid"`: a stored key that is not in the model makes reads fail (500). Add the field to the model or migrate the data; do not loosen the generated model.
- Style: Python 3.12, `from __future__ import annotations`, type hints everywhere, ruff clean (line 110) and `ruff format`; async all the way (no blocking IO in handlers or hooks). Turkish docstrings / comments are fine; identifiers in English.

## Tests

- Every module has `tests/modules/<m>/test_admin_crud.py` (written by the first generate, then yours). It runs on the skeleton's `tests/conftest.py` fixtures (`client`, `make_token`, `mock_db`; mongomock, no real Mongo). When you add a hook rule, a field or change a default, update the expectations there (`body()`, `minimal_expected()`, `INVALID_CREATE`, …) and add a test for the rule; never delete a failing assertion to get green.
- If the file was written with `pytestmark = skip` (no sample value for a field's `pattern`), fill `body()` / `minimal_body()` and remove the skip.
- mongomock cannot compare / sort `Decimal128`; decimal range and sort belong in a real-Mongo test.
- Before finishing: `uv run pytest -q`, `uv run ruff check src tests`, `uv run ruff format --check src/<pkg>/modules tests/modules`, `uv run lint-imports`.

## Generator side (this repo)

- Decisions live in `pythonContext.ts` (module files) and `pythonTestContext.ts` (module test values); templates only print prepared lines. Line wrapping via `pythonFormat.ts` (`pyCall`, `pyDef`, `pyLitLines`): generated G files and the module test must stay `ruff check` + `ruff format` clean.
- G files through `writePythonGenerated` (skips header-less files); K files, assets and the module test through `writeOnce`.
- Gates: `node scripts/verify/python-e2e.mjs` (regen-python, python-bootstrap, python-import, Python parity); for a quick loop `regen-python.mjs --no-docker --no-stockexchange`.
